# draft
// FIRST DRAFT (phase 2): rewrite or sign off. Voice: docs/voice.md. Flags: docs/story-drafts.md.
Skögul is on her feet before you hear anything. She brushes the crumbs off her tunic, then brushes them off again.
The dead fall silent. A woman in a cloak of falcon feathers walks the length of the queue, and they turn to watch her like flowers after the sun.
She stops at your table, picks up your stamp and turns it over, as if she's never seen one. She probably hasn't. Other people stamp for her.
"You're the new chooser. Skögul says you're careful." # speaker: freyja
"Half the slain are mine by right. Odin forgets that when it suits him. From today I name a whim each morning, and the worthy who match it come to Fólkvangr." # speaker: freyja
"My field is wide and the mead is sweet, and nobody there has to get up early to fight." # speaker: freyja
* ["Yes, lady."]
  "Good. I remember the ones who remember me." # speaker: freyja
  # fx: standing freyja +1
* ["I stamp by Odin's rules."]
  "Then Odin's rules now include me. Read the decree, little chooser." # speaker: freyja
  # fx: standing odin +1
  # fx: standing freyja -1
- She puts your stamp down exactly where it was, which is somehow worse than if she'd dropped it.
She leaves behind a smell of apples and cold iron. Skögul lets out a breath.
"Two masters now," she says. "Don't get between them." # speaker: skogul
"The whim is on the decree. Red hair, a left hand, amber: whatever takes her fancy that morning. A worthy soul who matches it is hers. One who doesn't is still Odin's." # speaker: skogul
She goes back to her bread, and doesn't eat it.
-> END
